1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,260
Listen to a talk in a psychology class.

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:11,030
Resilience refers to the ability to adapt and recover from adversity or stress.

3
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:21,050
It's a dynamic process that varies significantly from person to person influenced by a combination of genetic, psychological and social factors.

4
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:26,020
Research has shown that certain traits and behaviors can enhance resilience.

5
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:29,980
These include optimism, the ability to regulate emotions

6
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,180
and having a strong support network.

7
00:00:32,180 --> 00:00:38,521
For instance, people who maintain a positive outlook are better equipped to handle setbacks

8
00:00:38,521 --> 00:00:43,050
because they tend to see challenges as temporary and surmountable.

9
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:47,832
Emotional regulation involves managing one's feelings in a healthy way

10
00:00:47,832 --> 00:00:51,180
which can prevent stress from becoming overwhelming.

11
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:56,220
Moreover, social connections play a crucial role in resilience.

12
00:00:56,220 --> 00:01:00,760
Support from family and friends can provide emotional comfort

13
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:04,019
and practical assistance during difficult times.

14
00:01:04,019 --> 00:01:08,825
Communities with strong social bonds typically exhibit higher levels of collective resilience

15
00:01:08,825 --> 00:01:13,230
which is the ability of a group to recover from crisis.

16
00:01:13,230 --> 00:01:18,590
Next, we will discuss various strategies that individuals can use to build

17
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:21,270
and strengthen their resilience over time.
